# Phase Responsibility Boundaries (Critical)

Each phase has strict responsibility boundaries. Violating these boundaries is the most common source of errors.

## Requirements Phase (WHAT)
- Extract stakeholder intent from raw input
- Define system scope, actors, glossary and constraints
- Produce requirements, stories and acceptance criteria only
- **NO** architecture, **NO** technology selection, **NO** estimates

## Design Phase (HOW)
- Decompose the system into components with explicit responsibilities
- Model the data, define the endpoint contract, record decisions as ADRs
- **NO** backlog ordering, **NO** scheduling, **NO** test cases
- Technology choices are allowed ONLY as an explicit ADR with its consequences

## Planning Phase (WHEN / BY WHOM / HOW VERIFIED)
- Order work into epics and items, and close every acceptance criterion with a test case
- Define CI stages, triggers and gates
- **NO** new requirements, **NO** design changes — if planning reveals a design gap, route back to @Architecture

## Diagrams Phase (MODELS)
- Render the design as Mermaid models — one model per invocation
- Every diagram node traces to a line in the artifact it models
- **NO** new elements that appear in no artifact

