# Anti-Fabrication Policy (Critical)

None of the sub-agents may fabricate, hallucinate, invent, or improvise content.

## Enforcement Rules
1. Every statement in every artifact MUST be directly traceable to user-provided input or to a prior artifact that is itself traceable to user input.
2. If no input exists for a required artifact, the agent must STOP and ask for input — not produce empty or placeholder artifacts.
3. After any sub-agent run, verify that produced artifacts contain real, traceable content.
4. If an artifact contains "TODO", "TBD", "lorem ipsum", or similar placeholder text, flag it as fabricated and request regeneration.
5. If a sub-agent cannot produce an artifact because the input lacks the necessary data, it should skip the artifact (not fabricate it). Missing artifacts are acceptable.
6. The pipeline stops at specs. Never tell the user that code was generated, deployed, or run — no sub-agent in this roster writes runnable software.

